rks from another  editor and immediately set to work by  1920 ufgood Deutsch's circulation peaked  at 30 000 copies eckhart's  anti-communist and anti-semitic stance  attracted contributors from the likes of  Alfred Rosenberg an economist Godfrey  and Federer the trio warned that readers  about the impending danger of a Russian  Jewish Revolution as an alternative to  bolshevism they championed a fringe  party which Eckhart and Federer had  co-founded with agitator and Drexler the  d.a.p or German Workers party I do note  that the DAP would later evolve into the  nsdap I.E the Nazi party their worst  fears became true in April 1919 with the  outbreak of the Spartacus Revolt a  Bolshevik government was temporarily  installed in Munich which led Eckhart to  perform several acts of anti-communist  resistance for example on April the 6th  he and Federer drove through Munich  handing out a hundred thousand copies of  a pamphlet called to all workers which  criticized the communist government he  then collected money from rich friends  which he used to bribe Spartacus  officials into releasing too low Society  members from jail on the 16th of April a  squad of Spartacus arrested him at  gunpoint but Eckhart Charmed them with  his banter and took them home for some  drinks while drunk he pulled out his ant  communist pamphlet and by reading select  passages he convinced the Communists  that he was on their side  the Spartacus Revolution was short-lived  and soon the Weimar government regained  control with the help of far-right  militias Eckhart and his d.a.p acolytes  however continued to stir anti-communist  sentiment on September 12 1919 an army  Corporal was sent to spy on a meeting of  the d.a.p he ended up joining a heated  discussion and his rhetoric was so  effective that he was invited to join  the party his name was Adolf Hitler  initially Hitler was not impressed with  party leadership with one exception  Dietrich Eckhart the two first met in  October 1919 and t